[{:registry/operating-states [:intake :propose :approve :execute :audit] :actor/wave 2 :registry/required-technologies [:robotics :identity :audit-ledger] :actor/scope-excluded-ops [:finalize-route :override-route-decision :commit-to-route :determine-right-of-way :direct-traffic-navigation :override-driver-route-judgment :override-driver-on-road-judgment :decide-animal-fitness-for-work :determine-animal-fitness-for-work :authorize-veterinary-treatment :order-veterinary-treatment :override-driver-animal-handling-judgment :override-driver-safety-judgment] :actor/robotics? true :adr/related ["adr-2607121000-cloud-itonami-global-isic-isco-reverse-toposort-plan" "adr-2607152500-cloud-itonami-wave4-rollout-start-amendment" "adr-2799005411-cloud-itonami-isco-5411-firefighters-coverage" "adr-2799005413-cloud-itonami-isco-5413-prison-guards-coverage"] :adr/status :accepted :actor/scope-excluded-terms ["finalize the route" "finalized the route" "commit to the route" "committed to the route" "override the driver's route judgment" "overrode the driver's route judgment" "override the driver's on-road judgment" "overrode the driver's on-road judgment" "override the driver's on-road safety judgment" "overrode the driver's on-road safety judgment" "override the driver's animal-handling judgment" "overrode the driver's animal-handling judgment" "override the driver's safety judgment" "overrode the driver's safety judgment" "determine the animal's fitness for work" "determined the animal's fitness for work" "decide the animal was fit for work" "decided the animal was fit for work" "decide the animal's fitness for work" "decided the animal's fitness for work" "authorize the veterinary treatment" "authorized the veterinary treatment" "order the veterinary treatment" "ordered the veterinary treatment" "administer veterinary treatment" "administered veterinary treatment" "direct the traffic navigation" "directed the traffic navigation" "finalize the traffic-navigation decision" "finalized the traffic-navigation decision" "assign the right of way" "assigned the right of way" "make the right-of-way decision" "made the right-of-way decision" "ルートを確定した" "経路判断を上書きした" "運転手の路上判断を上書きした" "運転手の動物取扱判断を上書きした" "動物の就労適性を判定した" "獣医treatment を指示した" "交通誘導を指示した" "優先通行権を決定した"] :adr/id 2799009332 :phase/rollout "{0 {:label \"read-only\", :writes #{}, :auto #{}}, 1 {:label \"assisted-logging\", :writes #{:log-trip-record}, :auto #{}}, 2 {:label \"assisted-coordination\", :writes #{:log-trip-record :schedule-dispatch-operation :coordinate-maintenance-order}, :auto #{}}, 3 {:label \"supervised-auto\", :writes #{:log-trip-record :schedule-dispatch-operation :coordinate-maintenance-order :flag-welfare-concern}, :auto #{:log-trip-record :schedule-dispatch-operation :coordinate-maintenance-order}}}" :actor/domain :logistics/animal-drawn-vehicle-dispatch-and-logistics-coordination :actor/proposal-ops [:log-trip-record :schedule-dispatch-operation :flag-welfare-concern :coordinate-maintenance-order] :actor/hard-checks [:no-actuation :op-not-allowed :unknown-driver :driver-unverified :missing-depot-id :unknown-depot :depot-unverified :depot-mismatch :trip-record-decision-forbidden :dispatch-schedule-override-forbidden :scope-excluded] :registry/maturity :implemented :actor/isco-08 "9332" :actor/always-escalate-ops [:flag-welfare-concern] :adr/doc_type "adr" :operation/nodes [:intake :advise :govern :decide :request-approval :commit :hold] :operation/entry-point :intake :adr/body "# ADR 2799009332: cloud-itonami ISCO-08 9332 Drivers of Animal-drawn Vehicles and Machinery dispatch/logistics coordination coverage\n\n## Status\n\nAccepted\n\n## Context\n\nThis is part of the occupation-classification track (sibling to the\n`cloud-itonami-isic-*` industry-actor rollout, same governing\nADR-2607121000): codify every ISCO-08 occupation unit group as an\nautonomous \"actor\" (LLM/advisor behind an independent Governor, a\n`langgraph.graph` StateGraph, append-only audit ledger), modeled on a\nrobotics premise -- a robot performs the occupation's physical/\nadministrative work, proposing actions to an independent Governor that\ngates them, never dispatches hardware itself, always escalates\nhigh-stakes decisions to a human. This ADR covers **ISCO-08 class 9332\n-- Drivers of Animal-drawn Vehicles and Machinery** only.\n\nThe `kotoba-lang/occupation` registry's live `{:id \"9332\" ...}` entry\nwas verified against a fresh clone before any work began (`clojure -M\n-e \"(require 'kotoba.occupation) (println (kotoba.occupation/get-\noccupation \\\"9332\\\"))\"` from a checkout with the `kotoba-lang/\ntechnology` sibling present at the correct `../technology` relative\npath), and its `:name` read exactly \"Drivers of Animal-drawn Vehicles\nand Machinery\" -- confirming the premise, no mismatch. Prior to this\nADR the entry's `:maturity` was `:spec` with `:required-technologies\n[:robotics :identity :audit-ledger]` and no `:repo`/`:business-id`; no\nrepository existed at `cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-9332` (`gh api`\n404 confirmed before scaffolding, and again immediately before repo\ncreation). This ADR and its companion registry edit promote the `9332`\nentry to `:implemented`.\n\n**This actor carries a dual safety dimension unique among this fleet's\ntransport-adjacent actors so far: BOTH a road-safety dimension (traffic\nnavigation) AND an animal-welfare dimension (the draft animal's\ntreatment/working conditions).** Drivers of animal-drawn vehicles work\ndirectly with draft animals on public roads, so a wrongful automated\ndecision could compound harm across two axes at once -- a route/traffic\nmisjudgment endangering road users, or a welfare/treatment misjudgment\nharming the animal. The controlling precedent is **ADR-2607152500**\n(Wave4 rollout start amendment), which established that decisions\ndirectly touching safety, dignity or subsistence must always exclude\nthe closed op allowlist and always escalate to a human, not merely be\ngated behind a confidence threshold. This ADR applies that guardrail\nshape to both axes simultaneously: no op anywhere in this actor's\nclosed allowlist may finalize a route/traffic-navigation decision,\ndecide an animal's welfare/treatment disposition, or override a\ndriver's on-road or animal-handling safety judgment.\n\nThe reference implementation mirrored for module SHAPE is\n[`cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-3313`](https://github.com/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-3313)\n(Accounting Associate Professionals: `store`/`advisor`/`governor`/\n`actor` split, `langgraph.graph` StateGraph, full doc set), cloned and\nread in full this session. The closed-allowlist + registered-AND-\nverified provenance + content-based scope-exclusion SAFETY PATTERN\nfollows the same shape already established by this fleet's other\nsafety-critical occupation actors in this same retry batch (ISCO-08\n5411 Firefighters and 5413 Prison Guards), adapted substantially to\nthis vertical's dual road-safety/animal-welfare guardrail rather than\nfollowing either domain shape directly.\n\n## Decision\n\nPublish `cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-9332` as an OSS\ndocumentation/logistics-coordination actor for drivers of animal-drawn\nvehicles and machinery, following the SAME governed-actor architecture\nas every prior `cloud-itonami-isco-*` actor in this fleet: **Dispatch\nLogistics Advisor ⊣ CartageGovernor** on a `langgraph.graph`\nStateGraph (`io.github.kotoba-lang/langgraph`, git-sha-pinned\nidentically to the reference's `deps.edn` -- this is a different\nlibrary coordinate from the `langgraph-clj` used by the unrelated\n`20-actors/*` actor family), with an independent Governor,\nhuman-in-the-loop approval via `interrupt-before`, and an append-only\naudit ledger.\n\nThis actor is deliberately **dispatch/logistics scheduling\ncoordination ONLY, never vehicle-operation or animal-handling\nauthority** -- it must NEVER be designed to exercise, simulate\nexercising, or propose exercising ANY of: a route/traffic-navigation\ndecision, an animal-welfare/treatment decision, or an override of a\ndriver's on-road or animal-handling safety judgment. These are not\nmerely gated behind escalation -- they are structurally absent from the\nop-allowlist entirely, and enforced a second, independent way via a\ncontent-based scope-exclusion check over free text.\n\n### Closed proposal-op allowlist (all `:effect :propose`)\n\n- `:log-trip-record` -- trip/fare/animal-condition-check-in data\n  logging (metadata only -- trip id, fare amount, animal condition\n  check-in, timestamp -- NEVER a route decision or a treatment\n  decision)\n- `:schedule-dispatch-operation` -- driver-roster/route-assignment\n  scheduling proposal (advance scheduling logistics only -- never a\n  live traffic-navigation override or a real-time driver-judgment\n  override)\n- `:flag-welfare-concern` -- surface a vehicle-defect/road-hazard/\n  animal-welfare concern, ALWAYS escalates immediately, NEVER\n  auto-commit-eligible\n- `:coordinate-maintenance-order` -- vehicle/harness maintenance\n  procurement proposal, escalates above a registered per-depot cost\n  threshold\n\nThis actor has **NO op, anywhere in its allowlist, that resembles**: a\nroute/traffic-navigation decision, an animal-welfare/treatment\ndecision, or an override of a driver's on-road or animal-handling\nsafety judgment. These are **structurally absent from the op-allowlist\nentirely**, not merely gated behind escalation -- an op such as\n`:finalize-route` or `:decide-animal-fitness-for-work` cannot even be\nproposed by the reference mock advisor (its `infer` function only ever\nemits one of the four allowlist ops, driven by a `case` expression with\nno default branch producing any other op shape), and if any code path\n(a forged proposal, a future LLM advisor, a misbehaving fork) ever\nproduced such an op, the governor's closed-allowlist HARD check\n(`:op-not-allowed`) rejects it unconditionally and permanently.\nVerified two ways: (a) unit tests directly against `governor/check` for\ntwelve concretely-named forbidden op fixtures\n(`cartage.governor/scope-excluded-ops`: `:finalize-route`,\n`:override-route-decision`, `:commit-to-route`,\n`:determine-right-of-way`, `:direct-traffic-navigation`,\n`:override-driver-route-judgment`,\n`:override-driver-on-road-judgment`,\n`:decide-animal-fitness-for-work`,\n`:determine-animal-fitness-for-work`,\n`:authorize-veterinary-treatment`, `:order-veterinary-treatment`,\n`:override-driver-animal-handling-judgment`,\n`:override-driver-safety-judgment`), and (b) an END-TO-END test that\ndrives each of those same twelve ops through a ROGUE advisor and the\nFULL `langgraph.graph` actor graph (not just the governor's pure check\nfunction), proving the StateGraph itself always resolves to `:hold`\nwith zero records committed even when the advisor node itself is\ncompromised\n(`cartage.actor-test/holds-every-scope-excluded-op-attempt-even-via-a-rogue-advisor`).\n\n### Seven HARD governor checks (permanent, un-overridable)\n\n1. **Driver unregistered/unverified** -- any proposal must resolve to\n   an independently `:verified?` driver/permit-holder record. Never\n   trusts the proposal's own claim of who the driver is. Directly\n   implements the task's \"driver/permit record must be independently\n   verified/registered before any action\" invariant for the driver\n   half.\n2. **Effect not `:propose`** -- any other `:effect` value is a HARD\n   block (a claim to directly actuate outside governance -- the\n   governor never dispatches hardware, never operates the vehicle,\n   never directly handles the animal).\n3. **Op not allowed** -- any `:op` outside the closed four-op allowlist\n   is a HARD, PERMANENT block. This independently rejects any attempt\n   to slip in a route-finalization/right-of-way/animal-fitness/\n   veterinary-treatment/driver-judgment-override-shaped op.\n4. **Depot basis** -- `:log-trip-record`, `:schedule-dispatch-\n   operation` and `:coordinate-maintenance-order` must cite a\n   REGISTERED AND VERIFIED depot matching the driver's own depot\n   (`:missing-depot-id` / `:unknown-depot` / `:depot-unverified` /\n   `:depot-mismatch`). `:flag-welfare-concern` is deliberately EXEMPT\n   from this check -- it is the channel by which a brand-new depot, or\n   an urgent welfare concern with no depot on file yet, is surfaced for\n   human intake, so it must not be blocked on the very depot record it\n   exists to help flag.\n5. **Trip-record decision forbidden** -- `:log-trip-record` is a\n   trip/fare/animal-condition-check-in metadata record ONLY. Any\n   proposal carrying a route/traffic-navigation-decision or\n   animal-welfare/treatment-decision field\n   (`cartage.governor/log-record-forbidden-keys`: `:route-decision`,\n   `:route-finalization`, `:navigation-override`,\n   `:right-of-way-decision`, `:traffic-priority-decision`,\n   `:treatment-decision`, `:veterinary-treatment-order`,\n   `:fitness-for-work-decision`, `:welfare-disposition`) is a HARD,\n   PERMANENT block -- this actor never records a route decision or a\n   treatment decision, only metadata check-ins.\n6. **Dispatch-schedule override forbidden** -- `:schedule-dispatch-\n   operation` is driver-roster/route-assignment scheduling logistics\n   ONLY. Any proposal carrying a live traffic-navigation-override or\n   driver-judgment-override field\n   (`cartage.governor/schedule-forbidden-keys`:\n   `:route-navigation-directive`, `:traffic-priority-override`,\n   `:right-of-way-assignment`, `:on-road-judgment-override`,\n   `:animal-handling-judgment-override`, `:navigation-command`,\n   `:treatment-decision`, `:fitness-for-work-decision`) is a HARD,\n   PERMANENT block -- this actor never overrides a driver's real-time\n   on-road or animal-handling judgment, it only schedules which\n   driver/vehicle is assigned to which route slot in advance.\n7. **Scope exclusion** -- independent, defense-in-depth layer on top of\n   checks 3/5/6: even for an otherwise-allowed op, any proposal whose\n   free text (`:rationale` or `:note`) names a finalization/execution\n   ACTION for a route/traffic-navigation decision, an animal-welfare/\n   treatment decision, or an override of the driver's on-road or\n   animal-handling safety judgment\n   (`cartage.governor/scope-excluded-terms`, e.g. \"finalize the\n   route\", \"override the driver's route judgment\", \"determine the\n   animal's fitness for work\", \"order the veterinary treatment\", plus\n   Japanese equivalents) is a HARD, PERMANENT block, evaluated\n   unconditionally on content.\n\n### Two escalation gates, plus the general confidence floor\n\n- `:flag-welfare-concern` -- ALWAYS escalates to a human, regardless of\n  confidence (governor's `always-escalate-ops`). This is the ONLY\n  channel by which the robot may surface an observation suggesting a\n  vehicle defect, road hazard, or animal-welfare concern needs human\n  attention -- it never resolves the observation itself, and the\n  robot's role ends at \"here is the trip/roster/condition-check-in\n  status,\" never \"here is where to drive\" or \"here is whether the\n  animal is fit to work.\"\n- a `:coordinate-maintenance-order` proposal whose `:cost` exceeds\n  `maintenance-cost-escalation-threshold` (800, inclusive boundary\n  verified by `ok-at-exact-maintenance-cost-threshold-boundary`) --\n  always needs human sign-off, independent of confidence. This is an\n  ESCALATION, not a hard block: an over-budget maintenance order (e.g.\n  a full harness-set replacement) is not itself unsafe, unlike a\n  route/traffic-navigation, animal-welfare/treatment, or driver-\n  judgment-override attempt, which is why it is handled by a different\n  mechanism (soft escalate vs. structural absence).\n- (advisor confidence below `confidence-floor` 0.6 also escalates, for\n  any op.)\n\n### Self-trip guard (fleet-known bug class)\n\nA governor's scope-exclusion term list phrased as a bare noun (e.g.\n\"route\", \"welfare\") can accidentally match inside the mock advisor's\nown default rationale text for a legitimate proposal, self-blocking the\nactor's own happy path. This risk is especially sharp here because this\nactor's own op is literally named `:flag-welfare-concern` -- a bare\n\"welfare\" term would self-trip on every single legitimate welfare-flag\nproposal. `cartage.governor/scope-excluded-terms` is phrased\nexclusively as finalization/execution ACTIONS (e.g. \"finalize the\nroute\", \"override the driver's route judgment\", \"determine the\nanimal's fitness for work\" -- the exact phrasing pattern given in the\ntask's guidance on this known bug class), never bare nouns, and\n`cartage.governor-test/default-mock-advisor-proposals-never-self-trip-\nscope-exclusion` is a dedicated regression test asserting every op in\nthe closed allowlist (including both the depot-present and depot-nil\nvariants of `:flag-welfare-concern`), driven through the default mock\nadvisor, never trips `:scope-excluded` or `:op-not-allowed`. The mock\nadvisor's own default rationale template (\"documented <op> for depot\n<id>\" / \"documented <op> (no depot yet -- new-depot intake)\") was\nwritten to avoid any bare-noun collision by construction. Green on\nfirst run this session -- the scope-exclusion self-trip guard itself\nwas never tripped during development or verification.\n\n## Consequences\n\n- `kotoba-lang/occupation` registry's `{:id \"9332\" ...}` entry promoted\n  from `:spec` to `:implemented`, with `:repo`/`:business-id` set to\n  the real repository\n  (`https://github.com/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-9332` /\n  `cloud-itonami-isco-9332`), and `maturity-summary`'s implemented\n  count bumped accordingly (recomputed live from the registry via\n  `kotoba.occupation/maturity-summary`, not assumed, immediately before\n  the edit to account for concurrent sibling landings in this same\n  retry batch).\n- Full test suite (`clojure -M:test`): 45 tests, 154 assertions, 0\n  failures, 0 errors -- raw output captured in this ADR's\n  `:test/counts` and in the task report, independently re-verified\n  against a brand-new fresh clone of the pushed repository (not just\n  the local working copy).\n- No implementation bug was found during this session's verification\n  pass -- the test suite was green on first run against both the local\n  working tree and the fresh post-push clone.\n- No `manifest/west.yml` changes -- this actor is registered purely via\n  the `kotoba-lang/occupation` capability registry, consistent with\n  sibling `cloud-itonami-isco-*`/`cloud-itonami-isic-*` actors.\n- No `kotoba-lang/technology` dependency was added to the actor's\n  `deps.edn` -- only the central `kotoba-lang/occupation` registry\n  itself depends on it, to resolve `:required-technologies` stacks.\n- This ADR is EDN-only, matching the live `90-docs/adr` convention\n  (commit `6d2d0eeda658`, \"Remove all .md, normalize ADRs to\n  tx-data\") -- a single-entity EDN vector with an `:adr/body` string\n  blob rather than a paired `.md`+`.edn`.\n- Full doc set published: README.md, CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md,\n  CONTRIBUTING.md, GOVERNANCE.md, SECURITY.md, LICENSE\n  (AGPL-3.0-or-later, byte-identical to the `cloud-itonami-isco-3313`\n  reference's LICENSE text), docs/business-model.md,\n  docs/operator-guide.md, blueprint.edn.\n\n## Alternatives considered\n\n- Giving the actor an op like `:approve-route-decision`/`:approve-\n  animal-treatment` that is merely gated behind `always-escalate-ops`\n  (the shape `cloud-itonami-isco-3313` uses for `:approve-over-\n  ceiling-posting`, or the shape a naive reading of \"gate high-stakes\n  actions behind human approval\" might suggest): rejected outright per\n  the task's explicit guidance and the `ADR-2607152500` precedent -- an\n  always-escalate op still means the *capability* to finalize a route\n  or a treatment decision exists in the code path and is merely\n  deferred to a human gate. For decisions carrying both a road-safety\n  and an animal-welfare dimension, the capability itself must not\n  exist. The only op related to escalating a concern is\n  `:flag-welfare-concern`, which surfaces the need for human attention\n  and never itself decides, authorizes, or defers a route/treatment\n  action for later automatic execution.\n- A bare-noun scope-exclusion term list (e.g. `[\"route\" \"welfare\"\n  \"judgment\"]`): rejected outright per the fleet-known self-trip bug\n  class described above -- this actor's own op is literally named\n  `:flag-welfare-concern`, so a bare \"welfare\" term would self-trip on\n  every legitimate welfare-flag proposal, and a bare \"route\" term would\n  self-trip on every legitimate dispatch-scheduling proposal (which\n  necessarily references route-related fields like `:route-id`).\n- Merging `driver` and `depot` into a single entity (only checking one\n  provenance record): rejected -- the depot-mismatch check requires two\n  independently registered-AND-verified entities so that a depot record\n  a driver is not assigned to is caught even if both records\n  individually pass verification.\n- A numeric confidence-only gate for `:log-trip-record` /\n  `:schedule-dispatch-operation` (no forbidden-keys content checks):\n  rejected as insufficient -- confidence measures the advisor's\n  certainty about the *proposal it chose to make*, not whether that\n  proposal smuggles forbidden content; a high-confidence advisor could\n  still misuse an allowed op's field shape to carry a forbidden route\n  decision or treatment decision, which is exactly why checks 5/6 exist\n  as independent, content-based, permanent HARD blocks regardless of\n  confidence.\n\n## Itemized safety confirmation\n\nEvery op in this actor's closed proposal-op allowlist, and why it is\nsafe under the constraints above:\n\n1. **`:log-trip-record`** -- trip/fare/animal-condition-check-in\n   metadata only (trip id, fare amount, animal condition check-in,\n   timestamp). Cannot carry a route decision or a treatment decision\n   (HARD-blocked by check 5, `:trip-record-decision-forbidden`, on a\n   closed forbidden-key list). Not a route/traffic-navigation decision\n   or an animal-welfare/treatment decision in any respect -- it is a\n   records-management action indistinguishable in kind from a dispatch\n   clerk's log entry.\n2. **`:schedule-dispatch-operation`** -- driver-roster/route-assignment\n   scheduling logistics only (route id, proposed time, vehicle id).\n   Cannot carry a live traffic-navigation override or a real-time\n   driver-judgment override (HARD-blocked by check 6,\n   `:dispatch-schedule-override-forbidden`, on a closed forbidden-key\n   list). Does not direct, override, or draw any conclusion about a\n   live on-road or animal-handling decision -- it is a calendar action\n   deciding in advance which driver/vehicle is assigned to which route\n   slot.\n3. **`:flag-welfare-concern`** -- surfaces a vehicle-defect/road-\n   hazard/animal-welfare concern to a human; ALWAYS escalates\n   (governor's `always-escalate-ops`, unconditionally, at every\n   confidence level), NEVER auto-commit eligible. This is the ONLY\n   channel through which such a concern may be surfaced, and it\n   explicitly never resolves, decides, or acts on anything itself --\n   the human reviews and acts entirely on their own authority.\n4. **`:coordinate-maintenance-order`** -- vehicle/harness maintenance\n   procurement proposal (item, cost, vendor). Gated by ordinary\n   cost-ceiling escalation (above 800 always escalates). Not a\n   road-safety or animal-welfare action of any kind -- it is a\n   purchasing-logistics action for vehicle/harness upkeep.\n\nNo op in this allowlist, and no op anywhere in this codebase, resembles\na route/traffic-navigation decision, an animal-welfare/treatment\ndecision, or an override of a driver's on-road or animal-handling\nsafety judgment -- these three categories are structurally absent, not\ngated, confirmed by: (a) the closed four-op allowlist itself\n(`cartage.governor/closed-op-allowlist`), (b) twelve concretely-named\nforbidden-op fixtures that are rejected at both the governor-unit level\nand the full-actor-graph level via a rogue advisor\n(`cartage.governor/scope-excluded-ops`,\n`cartage.governor-test/every-scope-excluded-op-name-is-rejected`,\n`cartage.actor-test/holds-every-scope-excluded-op-attempt-even-via-a-rogue-advisor`),\n(c) a content-based scope-exclusion check independent of the `:op`\nfield (`cartage.governor/out-of-scope?`,\n`cartage.governor/scope-excluded-terms`), tested end-to-end through a\nrogue advisor and the full compiled graph\n(`cartage.actor-test/holds-a-scope-excluded-rationale-attempt-even-via-a-rogue-advisor`),\nand (d) two additional content-shape guardrails preventing an\notherwise-allowed op from smuggling forbidden substance through its own\nfield shape (checks 5/6 above), both independently proven end-to-end\nvia a rogue advisor driving the full compiled StateGraph\n(`cartage.actor-test/holds-a-route-decision-attempt`,\n`cartage.actor-test/holds-a-dispatch-schedule-override-attempt`).\n" :adr/date "2026-07-17" :actor/cost-threshold-escalate-ops "{:coordinate-maintenance-order 800}" :test/counts "{:total 45, :assertions 154, :failures 0, :errors 0}" :actor/coordination? true :actor/name "Animal-drawn Vehicle Dispatch and Logistics Coordination Practice" :db/id -1 :test/coverage [:governor-hard-checks :advisor-shapes :integration :store-contract :scope-exclusion-self-trip-regression :driver-verification :depot-verification :closed-op-allowlist :maintenance-cost-threshold-escalation :trip-record-decision-forbidden :dispatch-schedule-override-forbidden :rogue-advisor-end-to-end] :registry/business-id "cloud-itonami-isco-9332" :registry/repo "https://github.com/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-9332" :adr/scope [:kotoba-lang/occupation :cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-9332] :test/simulator :cartage.actor-test :adr/title "cloud-itonami-isco-9332 — Drivers of Animal-drawn Vehicles and Machinery Dispatch/Logistics Coordination Coverage" :adr/source-format "edn" :adr/references [2607121000 2607152500] :actor/id :cloud-itonami-isco-9332}]
